  {
    "_createdAt": "2026-10-01T21:23:31Z",
    "_id": "31qLwPpZYSKIi7ZpC41EZp",
    "_rev": "seeJ8sDCx2bMNJQ2P1sTLT",
    "_type": "ingredient",
    "_updatedAt": "2026-10-03T18:17:36Z",
    "bild": {
      "_type": "image",
      "asset": {
        "_ref": "image-5719ae8cd08d3edcfbecbaa3afcb42ef40197722-1082x860-jpg",
        "_type": "reference"
      }
    },
    "description": {
      "_type": "localizedPortableText",
      "de": [
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-de-0",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-de-0",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Gochujang (고추장) ist eine dicke, fermentierte koreanische Chilipaste. Sie verbindet Schärfe, Süße und einen herzhaften Geschmack und eignet sich für Saucen, Marinaden und Pfannengerichte. Geschmack und Schärfe unterscheiden sich je nach Produkt."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-de-1",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-de-1",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Die passende Paste auswählen"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-de-2",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-de-2",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Achte auf die Bezeichnung Gochujang oder Korean Red Pepper Paste. Eine fertige Gochujang-Sauce kann bereits weitere Gewürze enthalten und ist nicht dieselbe Zutat wie die reine Paste im Rezept. Entscheidend sind Produktname und Schärfegrad, nicht die Farbe der Verpackung."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-de-3",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-de-3",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Gochujang oder Gochugaru?"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-de-4",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-de-4",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Gochujang ist eine gewürzte Paste. Gochugaru besteht aus getrockneten koreanischen Chiliflocken oder Chilipulver. Konsistenz und Verwendung sind unterschiedlich; die beiden Zutaten lassen sich nicht einfach löffelweise austauschen."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-de-5",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-de-5",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Wofür verwendet man Gochujang?"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-de-6",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-de-6",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Die Paste passt in Bibimbap-Sauce, Tteokbokki-Sauce und Marinaden. Für Chogochujang wird sie unter anderem mit Essig vermischt; bei Bokkeum Gochujang entsteht daraus eine gekochte Würzpaste. Die verlinkten Rezepte unten zeigen Mengen und Zubereitungsschritte."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-de-7",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-de-7",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Was eignet sich als Gochujang-Ersatz?"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-de-8",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-de-8",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Als Notlösung können Miso oder Doenjang mit koreanischen Chiliflocken und etwas Süße einzelne Geschmacksnoten annähern. Die Mischung ist kein gleichwertiger Ersatz. Vorsichtig abschmecken; wenn Gochujang das Gericht prägt, möglichst die Originalzutat verwenden."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-de-9",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-de-9",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Gochujang in Deutschland finden"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-de-10",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-de-10",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Suche in koreanischen oder asiatischen Lebensmittelgeschäften und bei Lebensmittel-Onlineshops mit Lieferung nach Deutschland nach Gochujang oder koreanischer Chilipaste. Prüfe Produktbeschreibung und Schärfegrad. Auch beim Einkauf in Deutschland lässt sich die Schärfe nicht allein aus dem Verkaufsland ableiten."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-de-11",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-de-11",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Nach dem Öffnen"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-de-12",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-de-12",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Beachte die Aufbewahrungshinweise auf der Packung, verschließe den Behälter und verwende einen sauberen Löffel."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        }
      ],
      "en": [
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-en-0",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-en-0",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Gochujang (고추장) is a thick, fermented Korean red pepper paste. It brings heat, sweetness and a savory depth to sauces, marinades and stir-fries. The balance varies between products, so choose the heat level that suits your cooking."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-en-1",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-en-1",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Choosing a paste for cooking"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-en-2",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-en-2",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Look for gochujang or Korean red pepper paste on the label. A ready-made gochujang sauce may already contain extra seasonings; it is different from the plain paste called for in a recipe. Check the product name and heat level rather than judging by the color of the tub."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-en-3",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-en-3",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Gochujang versus gochugaru"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-en-4",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-en-4",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Gochujang is a seasoned paste; gochugaru is dried Korean red pepper in flakes or powder. They have different textures and roles in a recipe, so do not swap them spoon for spoon."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-en-5",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-en-5",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "How to use it"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-en-6",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-en-6",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Mix it into the sauce for bibimbap, cook it into tteokbokki sauce, or use it in marinades. Chogochujang combines the paste with vinegar and other seasonings, while bokkeum gochujang turns it into a cooked condiment. Explore the linked recipes below for quantities and steps."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-en-7",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-en-7",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "What can replace gochujang?"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-en-8",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-en-8",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "In a pinch, miso or doenjang mixed with Korean chili flakes and a little sweetener can approximate some of its flavors. This is an improvised alternative, not the same paste. Adjust to taste; when gochujang is central to the dish, use the original ingredient if possible."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-en-9",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-en-9",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Where to look"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "gochujang-en-10",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "text-en-10",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Start with Korean or Asian grocery stores and online food retailers serving your country. Search for gochujang or Korean red pepper paste; check the product and delivery area before ordering."
